1
00:02:30,039 --> 00:02:35,399
This is the time known as the Great Pirate Era.

2
00:02:35,699 --> 00:02:39,699
A countless array of pirates go to battle across the seas in search of the One Piece,

3
00:02:39,959 --> 00:02:43,879
the legendary treasure left behind by Gold Roger, the King of the Pirates.

4
00:02:44,539 --> 00:02:48,759
Munkini and Luffy, a boy whose body turned to rubber after eating the gum-gum fruit,

5
00:02:49,059 --> 00:02:51,519
set sail to become the next King of the Pirates.

6
00:02:51,919 --> 00:02:54,479
As Luffy and his crew conquer numerous obstacles,

7
00:02:54,799 --> 00:02:57,639
they capture the unwanted attention of the world government,

8
00:02:57,639 --> 00:03:00,679
which will use any means necessary to stop them.

9
00:03:02,059 --> 00:03:03,439
This is exciting!

10
00:03:04,599 --> 00:03:07,279
Can't wait to see what kind of adventure's up next!

11
00:03:07,779 --> 00:03:11,039
With a charted course awash in danger and intrigue,

12
00:03:11,259 --> 00:03:15,299
the crew will cut a path across the Grand Line to the New World.

13
00:03:19,439 --> 00:03:24,339
After being separated from his crew, Luffy set out to rescue his captured brother, Ace.

14
00:03:24,339 --> 00:03:27,839
To do so, he snuck into the government prison, impelled down.

15
00:03:28,359 --> 00:03:31,259
With the assistance of Ivankov, the Queen of Newcomerland,

16
00:03:31,639 --> 00:03:33,679
Luffy was finally able to make it to level six,

17
00:03:33,819 --> 00:03:36,079
only to discover that Ace was already gone.

18
00:03:37,019 --> 00:03:39,559
I assure you, resistance is futile.

19
00:03:43,099 --> 00:03:43,619
Luffy!

20
00:03:44,159 --> 00:03:45,519
Your brother's a pirate.

21
00:03:45,959 --> 00:03:48,719
His fate was sealed the moment he stepped in this prison.

22
00:03:50,079 --> 00:03:50,959
Dammit, Luffy.

23
00:03:51,639 --> 00:03:53,479
I'd hoped Hancock was lying.

24
00:03:53,479 --> 00:03:56,899
It was a simple plan, but it defeated us nonetheless.

25
00:03:57,579 --> 00:04:00,119
As much as I hate to admit it, we're trapped here on level six,

26
00:04:00,359 --> 00:04:01,739
at least for the time being.

27
00:04:01,959 --> 00:04:03,659
As far as Ace Boy in the Navy goes,

28
00:04:03,779 --> 00:04:05,899
that ship has already sailed, literally.

29
00:04:06,519 --> 00:04:07,579
Give up on him, okay?

30
00:04:08,359 --> 00:04:10,399
Or rather, put your faith in Whitebeard.

31
00:04:10,559 --> 00:04:12,619
There's no way he'd give up on one of his own.

32
00:04:12,739 --> 00:04:13,679
He'll come up with something.

33
00:04:16,379 --> 00:04:17,179
I'm leaving.

34
00:04:17,519 --> 00:04:17,759
Huh?

35
00:04:17,759 --> 00:04:22,179
I'm going to Marineford.

36
00:04:22,899 --> 00:04:25,159
Look, if I give up now,

37
00:04:25,679 --> 00:04:27,259
I'll regret it.

38
00:04:27,259 --> 00:04:30,399
You can do as you like,

39
00:04:30,479 --> 00:04:31,199
but first of all,

40
00:04:31,279 --> 00:04:33,099
how do you propose we get off this floor?

41
00:04:35,419 --> 00:04:41,239
If you want out that bad,

42
00:04:41,319 --> 00:04:42,319
then set me free.

43
00:04:43,179 --> 00:04:44,879
I'll make a hole in the ceiling

44
00:04:44,879 --> 00:04:46,279
and you'll be free to go.

45
00:04:46,819 --> 00:04:47,659
Sound good?

46
00:04:47,659 --> 00:05:02,799
Crocodile!

47
00:05:02,799 --> 00:05:07,459
Just like old times, huh?

48
00:05:08,459 --> 00:05:09,979
Did you miss me?

49
00:05:09,979 --> 00:05:16,739
The ultimate team is formed!

50
00:05:17,059 --> 00:05:18,439
Shaking Impel down!

51
00:05:27,119 --> 00:05:30,159
You know, for the life of me,

52
00:05:30,239 --> 00:05:32,859
I couldn't think of a good reason to break out of here.

53
00:05:33,079 --> 00:05:36,219
But Whitebeard and the Navy are going to start a war?

54
00:05:36,219 --> 00:05:40,359
This is my chance to bring down that old man once and for all.

55
00:05:42,379 --> 00:05:45,059
This clash of powers has piqued my interest.

56
00:05:45,839 --> 00:05:48,159
And I've just the tools at my disposal

57
00:05:48,159 --> 00:05:50,279
to get us a front row seat to the action.

58
00:05:50,839 --> 00:05:53,039
You scratch my back and I'll scratch yours.

59
00:05:53,439 --> 00:05:55,359
Not a bad proposition, is it?

60
00:05:55,359 --> 00:06:12,939
Screw that crap!

61
00:06:13,199 --> 00:06:15,159
You messed up Phoebe's whole country, you jerk!

62
00:06:15,219 --> 00:06:16,019
You can rock down here!

63
00:06:16,019 --> 00:06:17,059
That was a long time ago.

64
00:06:17,359 --> 00:06:19,579
That place is no longer of any interest to me.

65
00:06:19,579 --> 00:06:28,139
However you may feel, we still need his help.

66
00:06:28,559 --> 00:06:30,699
If we have an opportunity to escape from here,

67
00:06:30,799 --> 00:06:32,139
then we're obliged to take it.

68
00:06:32,219 --> 00:06:32,559
What?

69
00:06:33,099 --> 00:06:34,179
Are you crazy, Eva?

70
00:06:34,379 --> 00:06:35,299
Do you know what this guy...

71
00:06:35,299 --> 00:06:36,499
There's no time to be hoity-toity.

72
00:06:37,179 --> 00:06:39,499
Sandy Pants here is our only ticket outside.

73
00:06:40,439 --> 00:06:41,819
Hello, Ifankov.

74
00:06:41,959 --> 00:06:43,799
My, my, it's been a long time.

75
00:06:43,959 --> 00:06:45,219
Eh, Crocoboy?

76
00:06:45,419 --> 00:06:46,939
Hey, wait, you two know each other?

77
00:06:47,139 --> 00:06:48,599
Just a passing acquaintance.

78
00:06:48,599 --> 00:06:51,479
I met him when he was a rookie, all wet behind the ears.

79
00:06:51,659 --> 00:06:52,619
I wouldn't worry.

80
00:06:53,179 --> 00:06:54,899
If this guy tries to double-cross us,

81
00:06:54,939 --> 00:06:56,599
I'll whip him into shape in a jiffy.

82
00:06:56,879 --> 00:06:58,899
As long as I've got an eye on him,

83
00:06:59,279 --> 00:07:01,299
then he should behave just fine.

84
00:07:02,899 --> 00:07:04,499
He is a scoundrel,

85
00:07:04,619 --> 00:07:06,939
but he's a scoundrel with a weakness I know well.

86
00:07:06,959 --> 00:07:09,519
Hey, if you so much as mention a word of that, I'll...

87
00:07:09,519 --> 00:07:10,379
Easy there.

88
00:07:10,539 --> 00:07:13,139
Sure you want to take that snippy tone with me, Crocoboy?

89
00:07:13,719 --> 00:07:15,159
Because I'd be more than happy

90
00:07:15,159 --> 00:07:17,359
to reveal your sordid past right now.

91
00:07:17,359 --> 00:07:17,859
Grr.

92
00:07:18,599 --> 00:07:20,299
Or you can shut that mouth of yours,

93
00:07:20,399 --> 00:07:20,999
help us out,

94
00:07:21,079 --> 00:07:23,199
and keep your dirty little secret.

95
00:07:24,419 --> 00:07:25,419
Hee-haw!

96
00:07:25,939 --> 00:07:26,499
Grr.

97
00:07:27,239 --> 00:07:28,099
Cocky bastard.

98
00:07:28,499 --> 00:07:30,039
Hey, you guys, while you're at it,

99
00:07:30,099 --> 00:07:31,499
you should let me out of here, too.

100
00:07:31,639 --> 00:07:32,739
Me, too, me, too!

101
00:07:32,899 --> 00:07:34,639
I got a boat to pick with Whitebeard!

102
00:07:34,739 --> 00:07:36,099
Yeah, let me out, too!

103
00:07:36,459 --> 00:07:37,039
Aw!

104
00:07:37,039 --> 00:07:40,699
Huh, huh, huh, huh, huh, huh, huh, huh, huh, huh, huh!

105
00:07:40,719 --> 00:07:41,979
Huh, huh, huh, huh, huh, huh, huh, huh, huh!

106
00:07:42,039 --> 00:07:42,359
Shut up!

107
00:07:43,059 --> 00:07:43,499
Shut up!

108
00:07:44,399 --> 00:07:45,419
Deaf-wing!

109
00:07:45,419 --> 00:07:51,759
Please, have mercy on me.

110
00:08:01,359 --> 00:08:03,339
I beg you to take me with you.

111
00:08:03,679 --> 00:08:05,239
I will be of great service.

112
00:08:05,779 --> 00:08:07,019
I've known your brother Ace

113
00:08:07,019 --> 00:08:08,979
since he first joined the Whitebeard Pirates.

114
00:08:09,259 --> 00:08:10,179
He's a good friend.

115
00:08:10,659 --> 00:08:13,479
And I know you too, from all the stories he's told.

116
00:08:13,479 --> 00:08:15,379
I'm not like the others down here.

117
00:08:15,619 --> 00:08:18,419
I was arrested because I objected to his execution.

118
00:08:20,819 --> 00:08:22,659
I want to help save Ace too.

119
00:08:22,859 --> 00:08:25,959
I swear, I will put my life on the line for him.

120
00:08:26,659 --> 00:08:27,559
Hmm.

121
00:08:27,559 --> 00:08:29,959
Jinbei, the first son of the sea.

122
00:08:30,559 --> 00:08:31,779
If they imprisoned him here,

123
00:08:31,779 --> 00:08:33,479
then he must have relinquished his title

124
00:08:33,479 --> 00:08:35,079
as one of the Seven Warlords.

125
00:08:35,479 --> 00:08:37,779
That would mean his self-proclaimed bond with Ace

126
00:08:37,779 --> 00:08:39,079
has merit indeed.

127
00:08:45,419 --> 00:08:52,379
All right, then.

128
00:08:52,579 --> 00:08:53,779
Wait, are you sure?

129
00:08:54,079 --> 00:08:55,419
You've never even met this man,

130
00:08:55,459 --> 00:08:57,159
and he's most assuredly dangerous.

131
00:08:57,379 --> 00:08:58,219
It'll be fine.

132
00:08:58,319 --> 00:08:59,379
Just let him out, okay?

133
00:09:01,759 --> 00:09:03,079
You have my gratitude.

134
00:09:03,079 --> 00:09:06,639
Me next!

135
00:09:06,739 --> 00:09:07,879
I like Ace too!

136
00:09:07,979 --> 00:09:09,339
I'll die for him and stuff!

137
00:09:09,439 --> 00:09:11,279
You boys are asking for a death!

138
00:09:11,279 --> 00:09:29,339
Two Warlords, or two former Warlords, that is.

139
00:09:29,739 --> 00:09:30,519
Wait a sec.

140
00:09:30,739 --> 00:09:31,379
This guy?

141
00:09:31,639 --> 00:09:32,199
For real?

142
00:09:32,199 --> 00:09:33,539
You won't regret this.

143
00:09:33,859 --> 00:09:35,259
I will fight to protect Ace,

144
00:09:35,339 --> 00:09:36,899
even if it means my own end.

145
00:09:38,299 --> 00:09:40,299
If you think you can stop the war

146
00:09:40,299 --> 00:09:41,739
between the Navy and Whitebeard,

147
00:09:41,819 --> 00:09:42,719
go ahead and try.

148
00:09:42,999 --> 00:09:44,659
I don't give a damn either way.

149
00:09:45,239 --> 00:09:47,859
As long as I get a shot at that crusty old bastard,

150
00:09:47,959 --> 00:09:48,899
it's worth it for me.

151
00:09:49,039 --> 00:09:50,999
If you think I'll let you lay a single finger

152
00:09:50,999 --> 00:09:52,599
on Whitebeard, you're wrong.

153
00:09:53,299 --> 00:09:55,839
Well, then, why don't you just try and stop me?

154
00:09:59,439 --> 00:10:01,999
Crocco Boy, your secret past,

155
00:10:01,999 --> 00:10:02,539
remember?

156
00:10:05,339 --> 00:10:06,539
It's settled, then.

157
00:10:06,959 --> 00:10:07,859
Let's get moving.

158
00:10:07,979 --> 00:10:09,099
We don't have much time.

159
00:10:09,339 --> 00:10:10,499
With a team this formidable,

160
00:10:10,659 --> 00:10:12,419
not even Impel Down can hold us.

161
00:10:12,719 --> 00:10:13,639
Yee-haw!

162
00:10:17,199 --> 00:10:18,739
All units, load up.

163
00:10:18,919 --> 00:10:19,459
Move out.

164
00:10:19,639 --> 00:10:20,799
Use your prison bullets.

165
00:10:21,559 --> 00:10:23,819
Prepare to deal with devil-proof powers.

166
00:10:24,519 --> 00:10:26,079
We've reached level six, sir.

167
00:10:26,479 --> 00:10:27,159
Move in!

168
00:10:31,999 --> 00:10:37,319
What the heck?

169
00:10:37,819 --> 00:10:39,259
Is that the ceiling?

170
00:10:39,639 --> 00:10:40,759
Worry about that later.

171
00:10:41,139 --> 00:10:42,599
Spread out and search the floor.

172
00:10:42,599 --> 00:10:47,199
Do you really think they stuck around here

173
00:10:47,199 --> 00:10:49,059
after making that gigantic hole,

174
00:10:49,239 --> 00:10:50,299
you morons?

175
00:10:50,299 --> 00:10:59,739
Shiryu!

176
00:10:59,959 --> 00:11:00,779
The jail manager!

177
00:11:02,679 --> 00:11:03,119
Pathetic.

178
00:11:03,559 --> 00:11:04,759
It's as plain as day.

179
00:11:05,159 --> 00:11:07,099
You can't do anything right without me.

180
00:11:07,459 --> 00:11:09,979
What a bunch of sorry excuses for jailers.

181
00:11:10,459 --> 00:11:11,579
Let me give you a hint,

182
00:11:11,759 --> 00:11:13,919
so maybe you can clean up this disgrace.

183
00:11:14,599 --> 00:11:15,839
While you were picking your noses,

184
00:11:15,839 --> 00:11:17,299
the three prisoners you're looking for

185
00:11:17,299 --> 00:11:18,959
released Crocodile and Jinbei.

186
00:11:20,179 --> 00:11:22,219
And then climbed up through that hole

187
00:11:22,219 --> 00:11:23,299
to level five.

188
00:11:23,879 --> 00:11:26,039
I want you to pass along a message for me.

189
00:11:26,659 --> 00:11:28,999
Tell Magellan I'll help him if he wants.

190
00:11:29,059 --> 00:11:30,299
No, that's, uh...

191
00:11:30,299 --> 00:11:32,879
What?

192
00:11:33,299 --> 00:11:34,199
What did you say?

193
00:11:34,319 --> 00:11:36,699
They've escaped with Jinbei and Crocodile?

194
00:11:36,799 --> 00:11:37,239
Yes, sir.

195
00:11:37,419 --> 00:11:38,499
They're not in their cells.

196
00:11:38,719 --> 00:11:39,139
No!

197
00:11:39,539 --> 00:11:41,919
Are you saying that even after my brilliant plan,

198
00:11:41,999 --> 00:11:44,139
they somehow weren't their way out of level six?

199
00:11:44,139 --> 00:11:46,779
And then now they're a group of five roaming wild

200
00:11:46,779 --> 00:11:48,719
and not sleeping like they're supposed to be?

201
00:11:48,899 --> 00:11:49,499
Yes, sir.

202
00:11:49,599 --> 00:11:50,239
That's correct.

203
00:11:52,399 --> 00:11:55,079
Do you think I might be held responsible

204
00:11:55,079 --> 00:11:56,179
for any of this nonsense?

205
00:11:56,179 --> 00:11:57,959
One, Magellan is currently transporting

206
00:11:57,959 --> 00:11:59,439
Portkis DAs to the Navy,

207
00:11:59,659 --> 00:12:02,499
so I'm afraid you'd be responsible for all of it.

208
00:12:02,639 --> 00:12:04,659
I knew you were gonna say that!

209
00:12:06,339 --> 00:12:07,139
All right.

210
00:12:07,219 --> 00:12:08,499
I'm gonna get out there and fight, too.

211
00:12:09,119 --> 00:12:11,239
All jailers report to level four immediately.

212
00:12:11,819 --> 00:12:12,859
Mistress Sadie, Salda.

213
00:12:12,859 --> 00:12:14,439
Gather your forces

214
00:12:14,439 --> 00:12:16,019
and head to level four this instant.

215
00:12:16,119 --> 00:12:18,339
I'll be warden even if I have to risk my life.

216
00:12:18,659 --> 00:12:19,839
Wait, what am I saying?

217
00:12:20,119 --> 00:12:21,059
Stop those criminals

218
00:12:21,059 --> 00:12:22,779
even if you have to risk your lives!

219
00:12:33,659 --> 00:12:36,339
You ready to boogie, Bon Boy?

220
00:12:36,719 --> 00:12:37,199
Yes!

221
00:12:37,199 --> 00:12:38,619
Yes, I am, Eva!

222
00:12:38,779 --> 00:12:39,759
Are you sure?

223
00:12:40,119 --> 00:12:41,719
Emporio Energy Hormones

224
00:12:41,719 --> 00:12:43,779
only give you strength for one day.

225
00:12:44,279 --> 00:12:46,419
There will be side effects.

226
00:12:46,679 --> 00:12:47,179
I know.

227
00:12:47,699 --> 00:12:48,859
Go ahead and do it.

228
00:12:49,699 --> 00:12:51,099
I mean, what choice do I have?

229
00:12:51,299 --> 00:12:52,019
If I don't,

230
00:12:52,059 --> 00:12:53,699
I won't even be able to get off the floor.

231
00:12:53,859 --> 00:12:55,019
Yes, good point.

232
00:12:55,299 --> 00:12:56,699
Unless I wanted to carry you.

233
00:12:56,959 --> 00:12:58,139
Which, for the record,

234
00:12:58,239 --> 00:12:58,979
I do not.

235
00:12:59,979 --> 00:13:03,479
Emporio Energy Hormone!

236
00:13:03,479 --> 00:13:07,419
Yikes, right at the jimmies.

237
00:13:07,739 --> 00:13:08,239
Oopsie.

238
00:13:08,699 --> 00:13:09,919
Newcomer power!

239
00:13:10,319 --> 00:13:12,239
Bon, please don't die!

240
00:13:14,119 --> 00:13:15,499
Is everybody ready?

241
00:13:16,159 --> 00:13:17,099
Just so you know,

242
00:13:17,199 --> 00:13:19,239
even if we do make it to the top of the prison,

243
00:13:19,619 --> 00:13:21,679
we'll still be in for one hell of a fight.

244
00:13:21,939 --> 00:13:24,299
We're completely surrounded by the Calm Belt,

245
00:13:24,419 --> 00:13:26,659
which is impassable in any normal ship.

246
00:13:26,819 --> 00:13:28,639
We'll have to steal a Navy vessel

247
00:13:28,639 --> 00:13:30,359
if we want to go anywhere near their headquarters.

248
00:13:30,979 --> 00:13:33,459
That means we need more people to join our team.

249
00:13:33,699 --> 00:13:34,539
I know what you're thinking.

250
00:13:34,659 --> 00:13:35,639
We have lots already.

251
00:13:36,039 --> 00:13:37,099
But to be honest,

252
00:13:37,299 --> 00:13:38,959
some of you won't make it out alive.

253
00:13:39,159 --> 00:13:40,579
By the time we reach the top floor,

254
00:13:40,739 --> 00:13:42,479
many of you won't be there to see it.

255
00:13:42,799 --> 00:13:43,619
If you're captured,

256
00:13:43,739 --> 00:13:44,919
you'll be tortured to death.

257
00:13:45,299 --> 00:13:46,399
There will be no mercy.

258
00:13:46,879 --> 00:13:47,919
So if we want to survive,

259
00:13:48,019 --> 00:13:50,259
we need to set free as many prisoners as possible

260
00:13:50,259 --> 00:13:52,319
while we make our way from here to Level 1.

261
00:13:52,559 --> 00:13:53,779
Whether we like them or not,

262
00:13:53,839 --> 00:13:54,759
we'll need their help.

263
00:13:54,759 --> 00:13:57,159
If we can cause enough chaos to start a riot,

264
00:13:57,299 --> 00:13:58,979
it'll help keep those jailers occupied.

265
00:13:58,979 --> 00:14:01,179
That means our first step on each floor

266
00:14:01,179 --> 00:14:02,139
is to open the cells

267
00:14:02,139 --> 00:14:04,219
and let our new friends clear the way for us.

268
00:14:04,319 --> 00:14:05,679
So let's give these boys hell!

269
00:14:05,859 --> 00:14:07,939
